# Design System Component Guidelines

## Project Structure

### Type Organization

Component-related types should be separated and written in `src/types/components/`.

```
src/
├── components/
│   └── Button/
│       ├── index.tsx          # Component implementation
│       └── tokens.ts          # Design tokens (optional)
└── types/
    └── components/
        ├── index.ts           # Re-export all component types
        └── Button.ts          # Button-specific types
```

**Type file example:**

```typescript
// src/types/components/Button.ts
export type ButtonVariant = 'filled' | 'outlined' | 'text'
export type ButtonSize = 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'

export interface ButtonProps
  extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: ButtonVariant
  size?: ButtonSize
  children?: React.ReactNode
}
```

**Import in component:**

```typescript
// src/components/Button/index.tsx
import type { ButtonProps } from '@/types/components/Button'
```

**Benefits:**

- Clear separation between types and implementation
- Easy type reusability
- Prevents circular references
- Improves testing and documentation

