## Style Logic Separation

### Separate Style Functions from Components

**✅ Best Practice:**

```typescript
// Separated, testable, reusable
const getComponentStyles = (theme: Theme, variant: Variant, size: Size) => {
  return css({
    // Access theme tokens
    color: theme.colors[variant],
    padding: theme.spacing[size],
    borderRadius: theme.shape[size].borderRadius,
  })
}

const Component = ({ variant, size }) => {
  return (
    <Element css={(theme: Theme) => getComponentStyles(theme, variant, size)} />
  )
}
```

**Benefits:**

- Testable: Can test style logic independently
- Reusable: Can share across components
- Maintainable: Clear separation of concerns
- Type-safe: Full theme type inference

**❌ Avoid inline styles:**

```typescript
// ❌ Hard to test, not reusable
<Element css={css`font-size: 16px; color: blue;`} />
```

